    <p class="mp-lead center">Most bites don't come from being careless — they happen in the ten seconds between brushing past tall grass and noticing. A nymph the size of a poppy seed climbs aboard, finds bare skin, and you never feel a thing. Here's that same moment, frame by frame, with the mesh on instead: the tick lands, hits a wall of fabric, and never reaches you.</p>
