        <p>A barrier is only as good as its weakest gap — so every edge is built to close. The fabric is a tight, even weave with openings smaller than a nymph tick; the seams are bonded flat instead of loosely stitched; and every opening you pull through is locked down with elastic.</p>
        <ul class="mp-checklist">
